From 97fc35a50789166402b1c684c56b59b080f03ae0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: raold <868138+raold@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:06:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Pass Flame Leviathan for raids of bots by the Ulduar
 Teleporter

Flame Leviathan is a siege-vehicle fight bots cannot drive: playerbots
boards a vehicle only when the bot's master sits in one, and it has no
convoy, approach or ram movement. His Lightning Wall is the only way into
the rest of Ulduar and opens only on his death.

He is never fought, killed or credited: his row stays, skipped by design.
For a raid of bots only (no member a person controls), a conditional pass
(hook 69) moves every bot outside his gate to the Ulduar Teleporter's
Colossal Forge destination, spell 64028's target position, which the
teleporter offers only once he is dead. No loot, kill, achievement or boss
state comes of it, and every boss after him is fought for real; a group a
person is in keeps the gate. The pass is due on live state only, so it
also takes stragglers a restart or recall puts back at the entrance.

Razorscale hovers out of reach until a player tells the Expedition
Commander they are ready, so she gets a commander objective in front of
her and a ground anchor on her runway. Kologarn's Cache of Living Stone is
looted as an encounter chest. DcCapabilities.h advertises the pass.
